<h3 id=3D"adding-a-new-parking-spot-type">Adding a New Parking Spot Type</h=
3>
<p>The parking lot system is designed to support multiple parking spot type=
s (e.g., CompactSpot, RegularSpot, OversizedSpot). However, there may be a =
need to introduce a new type, such as a handicapped parking spot, to accomm=
odate specific requirements like accessibility. The challenge is to extend =
the system efficiently without modifying existing classes, adhering to the =
Open-Closed Principle (open for extension, closed for modification).</p>
<p>To achieve this, we can introduce a new HandicappedSpot class that imple=
ments the existing ParkingSpot interface. This approach ensures smooth inte=
gration with the system=E2=80=99s spot allocation and management logic, as =
ParkingManager already relies on the ParkingSpot interface for handling spo=
ts.</p>
